# Mileage Viewer - Login Configuration
#
# Copy this file to viewer.env (without the .example suffix) and fill in
# real values. viewer.env must NEVER be committed to version control.
#
# After editing, run "docker compose up -d mileage-viewer" to recreate
# the container; "docker compose restart" keeps the old values.
#
# Kept separate from .env on purpose: the viewer should not have a copy of
# the ingest auth token. Single-quote the hash as shown below so Compose
# preserves its '$' characters instead of interpolating them.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# VIEWER_USERNAME - whatever you want to log in as.
#
# VIEWER_PASSWORD_HASH - a werkzeug scrypt hash, NOT the password itself.
#   Build the image, then generate one (you'll be prompted for the
#   password; it isn't echoed and never gets written to disk):
#
#     docker compose build mileage-viewer
#     docker compose run --rm --no-deps mileage-viewer python -c \
#       "from getpass import getpass; \
#        from werkzeug.security import generate_password_hash as g; \
#        print(g(getpass('password: ')))"
#
#   ALWAYS wrap the result in single quotes below. The hash contains '$'
#   characters, and an unquoted value can get chewed up by shell or
#   Compose expansion. The service refuses to start if it detects this.
#
# VIEWER_SECRET_KEY - signs the session cookie. At least 32 characters;
#   empty or shorter values stop the viewer from starting. Generate with:
#
#     openssl rand -hex 32
#
#   Keep it stable. Changing it logs you out everywhere, and it must be
#   identical across gunicorn workers, which is why it lives here rather
#   than being randomly generated at startup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

VIEWER_USERNAME=replace-me-with-your-login-name
VIEWER_PASSWORD_HASH='replace-me-with-the-generate_password_hash-output'
VIEWER_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional endpoint address/place suggestions. Disabled when empty.
# Supply the complete /reverse URL of a self-hosted Nominatim instance or
# a Nominatim-compatible provider that permits private trip endpoints and
# persistent result caching. Use HTTPS for any provider outside your LAN.
# The public nominatim.openstreetmap.org service does NOT permit vehicle
# tracking applications and must not be used. No public service is a default.
# See server/README.md, "Endpoint place suggestions", before enabling.
VIEWER_GEOCODER_URL=
# Optional gap between successful calls, in seconds (range 0.1-60).
# Default: 1.1 s, which suits providers with a one-request-per-second policy.
# Values below 1 s are only for self-hosted Nominatim or a provider that
# explicitly permits them.
# VIEWER_GEOCODER_INTERVAL=
# Optional identifying User-Agent; use your provider's required contact format.
# This value goes only to the provider, not into pages or application logs.
VIEWER_GEOCODER_USER_AGENT=GPSMileageTracker/1.0
